+# Somerset airport notification and county-call source boundaries
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · **TEL03–TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05–TC06**. The newly acquired Team 8 Box 17 packet contains an FAA notification form, a traffic-management log and flight-handling records. The form records an operations-center notification and a weather notification. Separately, the Park Service cites county call transcripts from Recorder 1 and Recorder 3. No common call identifier was found in the checked FAA pages, so the county-call transfers and source recordings remain separate retrieval tasks. [Commission records finding aid](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/finding-aid.pdf) · [Exact ZIP member, reading scope and hashes](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## FAA source fields
+
+| Physical PDF locator | Observation |
+| --- | --- |
+| **P. 1**, form title and time-column images | FAA Form 8020-3, *Facility Accident/Incident Notification Record*, identifies **UAL 93**, handwritten **9/11/01**, and **Somerset County ARPT**. The Region Operations Center row appears to read **1451**, with overwriting in the time cell. The aviation weather row reads **1616**. A lower handwritten row reads **1507** in the time column. Its row label remains uncertain. The checked cells give no county-dispatch event identifier or demonstrated timebase. |
+| **P. 2**, lines 1–4 and 44 | The line above the log body begins **“Sep 12 12:00 2001”**. The printed operations heading reads **“TUESDAY SEPT 11, 2000”**. Both years are present in the page image. The body contains a **1409** entry for UAL93 reporting lost radar/primary near **2G9**. Preserve the header date and the entry time separately. This entry describes a traffic-management observation. |
+| **P. 3**, lines 8–12, 26–28, 50–59, and **p. 5**, lines 25–35, 66–76 | Preliminary notice fields show **2000Z** and **17:31**, respectively. The p. 3 departure time is **Unknown** and p. 5 gives **09/11/01 12:41**. Both give **1403** or **14:03** in their occurrence field. The p. 3 narrative says the data block went to coast track. P. 5 says the transponder was turned off. Those are different assertions in the two notices. Neither issuance sequence nor the actual source of either narrative is demonstrated here. |
+| **Pp. 6–7**, p. 6 line 2, p. 7 lines 12–13, 64–76 and 104–109 | The separate p. 6 page gives **9/11/01 5:31:00 PM UTC**. The December 6 report at p. 7 gives accident time **1403 GMT**. Its weather descriptions display **0954 EST** and **1054 EST**. Separate date/time fields display **1354 UTC** and **1454 UTC**. These are preserved as recorded. The form does not resolve the clock labels or link them to a county call. |
+
+[Commission ZIP mirror](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip) · [Page and text locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## County calls, transfer and retrieval
+
+- **Held FBI Packet 2, pp. 4–7, stamp 43 A–D.** The FBI records describe the Somerset DVD No. 60 copies and a Cambria cassette. The Cambria document reports a caller describing a crash and transfer to Somerset. The **10:18:43** and **10:02:27** times in that document are printed with separate incident-report descriptions. The transfer narrative gives no matching time field there. [FBI packet review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/8083c8214482e6b84484838c43a732e2aa12703e/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-doj-early-packet-delivery-2026-11-09/README.md)
+- **Park Service timeline, notes 95–98 and 101.** The timeline’s **10:03 a.m.** crash-call entry cites a Somerset Emergency Management Agency transcript, **Recorder 1**, with approximate timing. Note 96 cites **Recorder 3** and the Shanksville Volunteer Fire Company trip sheet. The **10:04 a.m.** timeline entry separately describes a **Westmoreland-to-Somerset** communication concerning a passenger call. It gives a different originating agency and reported subject from the Cambria transfer. Preserve both reports. The Park Service page is a later account and source locator. Its checked notes give no join to DVD No. 60 or either FBI copy. [Flight 93 National Memorial timeline and source notes](https://www.nps.gov/flni/learn/historyculture/september-11-2001-timeline.htm)
+- **Next discriminating records.** Obtain the Somerset Recorder 1 and 3 transcripts or media, the dated trip sheet, the two FBI copies, the Cambria cassette and the actual dispatch or transfer event identifiers. Match audio, routing and time fields across both ends before joining either reported transfer to a recording. For the FAA time and notice differences, seek the notification log, native traffic-management record and the preliminary-notice dispatch/version history.
+
+The FAA scan was acquired by validated byte range and checked against the ZIP index by path, length and CRC. All seven pages were screened and **21** PDF locators checked. Selected time, date and form fields were inspected in images. The **nine** Park Service text locators were checked against a body byte-identical to the one already held. Its general correction statement was addressed in the earlier FAA study. **PD01–PD04**, the corrected answer and its receipt, signed disposition and recommendation-specific outcomes remain open. No recording playback, calibrated clock comparison or call-leg join was performed. [Verification scope](SOURCE-PINS.json) · [Earlier FAA comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/tree/main/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-defense-ig-parallel-disposition-2026-11-05)
